1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock II — LeetCode 122

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,600
Problem: same prices, but now you can buy and sell as many times as you like — holding at most one share at a time.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,900
Example: prices = [7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4]

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,800
Buy 1 sell 5 (+4), buy 3 sell 6 (+3) → 7

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:14,450
Hint: all profit comes from rising runs, and a rise's profit is just the sum of its daily gains — so grab every step up

6
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:19,350
Approach: greedy — walk day by day, and whenever prices[i] > prices[i-1], add the difference to the profit

7
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:23,850
Start: maxProfit = 0; compare each day to the one before

8
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:26,340
Day 1: 1 > 7? no → skip

9
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:29,330
Day 2: 5 > 1 → bank +4, maxProfit = 4

10
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:31,820
Day 3: 3 > 5? no → skip

11
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:34,810
Day 4: 6 > 3 → bank +3, maxProfit = 7

12
00:00:34,810 --> 00:00:37,340
Day 5: 4 > 6? no → skip

13
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:39,740
Total profit = 4 + 3 = 7

14
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:44,330
Grab every rise → 7, versus 5 with a single trade. Time O(n), space O(1)

15
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:49,500
